15-bit Adder-Subtractor with Overflow Detector Circuit using Verilog
Oğuz Özbal 32673



Introduction:
This report explains how we design 15-bit Carry Lookahead Adder/Subtractor using Verilog. In this project, 15-bit CLA is built using 5 3-bit CLA blocks. It can perform both addition and subtraction, depending on the mode of the block. The design is tested using a testbench, which check for 8 different possibilities, such as carry and overflow.

Building Blocks:
This design built around two main pieces:
•	3-bit Carry Lookahead Adder (CLA_3bit):
o	Capable of 3-bit addition or subtraction.
o	Handles carry propagation and generation to speed up computations.
o	Capable of changing between subtraction (mode = 1) and addition (mode = 0) with mode input.
o	A 3-bit adder-subtractor is designed as building block for the 15-bit adder and it takes following inputs:
	Two 3-bit integers: C and D.
	A carry in Cin for the calculation.
	A mode signal to choose operation.
o	The outputs of this sub-module are:
	RES as 3-bit result.
	Cout as carry from the MSB.

•	15-bit Carry Lookahead Adder (CLA_15bit_top):
o	Uses 5 piece of CLA_3bit to achieve the 15-bit result.
o	Combines carry signals between alongside CLA blocks.
o	Includes overflow detection logic for addition and subtraction.
o	Capable of changing between subtraction (mode = 1) and addition (mode = 0) with mode input as well.
o	Inputs for this 15-bit CLA are:
	Two 15- bit integers A and B.
	A mode signal to choose operation.
o	The outputs of this top module are:
	S as the 15-bit result of the addition or subtraction.
	Cout as carry from the MSB.
	OVF, this is a flag for indicating if there is a signed overflow in the result.


Testbench and Testing Examples:

a. addition without a carry and without an overflow:
Inputs are A = 25, B = 50, mode = 0.

b. addition without a carry and with an overflow:
Inputs are A = 16000, B = 1000, mode = 0.

c. addition with a carry and without an overflow:
Inputs are A = 16000, B = -7999, mode = 0.

d. addition with a carry and with an overflow:
Inputs are A = -10000, B = -8000, mode = 0.

e. subtraction without a carry and without an overflow:
Inputs are A = 30, B = 100, mode = 0.

f. subtraction without a carry and with an overflow:
Inputs are A = 1, B = -16384, mode = 0.

g. subtraction with a carry and without an overflow:
Inputs are A = -8000, B = -12000, mode = 0.

h. subtraction with a carry and with an overflow:
Inputs are A = -16384, B = 2, mode = 0.

All the wanted testing scenarios are tested with these 8 different test cases.







